# Project conventions

- Treat tracked empty files as intentional placeholders. Fill them in place;
  do not invent parallel files or folders that duplicate the layout.
- Keep tooling config under `src/configs/` (Vite, Vitest, Playwright, ESLint,
  tsconfigs). Do not recreate those configs at the repo root.
- Preserve the `src-tauri/src/mdoels/` directory name unless explicitly asked
  to rename it (pre-existing typo; renaming breaks `mod` paths).
- Packaging is Windows-first (`src-tauri/nsis/`, `other/utilities/7zr.exe`).
- Prefer Node `.mjs` for agent/hook scripts over Bash/Python.

```text
❌ BAD: create vite.config.ts at repo root
✅ GOOD: edit src/configs/vite.config.ts
```
